# Deny by default — this file is for the dev image (`Dockerfile.dev`), which COPYes packages/ and
# nothing else: the rest of the base comes from Dockerfile's `base` target. The Dockerfile itself
# is whitelisted because BuildKit reads `-f <file>` from the context when it lives inside it.
*
!packages/
!tools/
packages/*/node_modules
!Dockerfile.dev

# Synology's metadata directories; they carry no build input and their files are newer than the
# compiled tree, which this image's staleness check would read as a forgotten build.
**/@eaDir
**/@eaDir/**
